<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Utah Territory</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1850">1850</a>–<a href="/years/1896">1896</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Also known as Territory of Utah</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/utah">Utah</a> Territory was an organised territory of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> created by the Compromise of 1850 from part of the lands taken from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico">Mexico</a>, replacing the Mormon-proposed State of Deseret. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brigham-young">Brigham Young</a> was its first governor until federal troops arrived in the Utah War of 1857–1858. Originally stretching from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/california">California</a> to the Rockies, it was reduced as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nevada">Nevada</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/colorado">Colorado</a> and Wyoming were formed, and it became the state of Utah in 1896.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/utah-territory.jpg" alt="Utah Territory" width="320" height="183" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mangoman88; Theshibboleth; Tsujigiri · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Utah_Territory,_vector_image_-_2011.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
